what's going on people in this video  i'll be breaking down a couple things  you might have missed in the teaser  trailer for my hero academia season six  and also be giving my reaction to the  news that the my hero manga is ending in  2022. at jump festa earlier today  hirokoshi officially confirmed that his  plan is to end the manga next year which  is obviously massive news however he did  leave open the small possibility that  things might continue a tiny bit longer  later in the video i'll be giving my  thoughts on what he said but first let's  break down the season 6 teaser trailer  ok so one of the first shots from this  trailer was this image of the paranormal  liberation front which is a new villain  organization led by shigaraki an  interesting thing to notice is that riy  destro is now using a walking stick  after his fight in the last season as  during his battle with shiguraki he was  forced to cut off his own feet to stop  his whole body from decaying since then  he's had prosthetic feet implanted  allowing him to walk when he's not using  his high-tech wheelchair  in the background we also have giganto  machia who is now wearing two arm  gauntlets which are more clearly visible  in the manga panel of this same moment  and of course in the center we have  shiguraki in his brand new style  as the successor to all for one him  wearing his suit is just a subtle way of  showing that he's ascended to that role  and just like afo his hair is now white  something that happened in the anime  last season after his awakening  moving on the teaser then goes on to  show us several glimpses of the heroes  getting ready for war with the villains  and without giving away spoilers it's  clear that the heroes have been split  into different locations  for example we have endeavor and his  group who were inside a building whereas  midoriya and his group are outside as  their job is to evacuate the civilians  from the city there's also a third team  of heroes who are somewhere else and on  the front lines you can see there's a  small group of students in particular  denki mudman mushroom girl and tamaki  amajiki in the back of this shot there's  a character with a handsaw for a head  and this is something that they've  changed from the manga because in  chapter 259 this same guy was actually  chainsaw man as in the real chainsaw man  from the manga of the same name this was  just a casual easter egg that harakoshi  included but for whatever reason he's  now hand saw man in the anime which i  imagine is a lot less effective  as a side note i read the chainsaw man  manga last year and i'd recommend it  because it was unlike anything i'd read  before especially towards the end it was  getting like really chaotic  and at the very least herikoji seems to  be a fan as well  anyway as the season 6 teaser continued  we got a brief look at the evil doctor  ujuko and all for one before the teaser  then ended on this shot of shigeraki  recovering inside a tank the last time  we saw this character he was being torn  apart by the doctor as part of an  experiment to enhance his body and  enhance his quirk ujko said that the  overall procedure would take four months  to complete and once that time was up  shigaraki would have the power to take  one for all  a large aspect of season six is the  heroes trying to prevent this fully  powered shigiraki from being completed  hence why this was likely the best shot  they could have ended the trailer on  without spoiling anything in the process  now in terms of hirokoshi's letter that  was read out of jamfester he revealed  that if things go to plan the my  academia manga will be complete within  one year while this is big news it's not  entirely surprising considering that  only seven months ago we got a chapter  titled the final act begins  from that moment we should have been  bracing ourselves for an announcement  like this as hirokoshi seems to now have  a solid idea of how the series will be  ending he went on to say that bakugou  will have a huge role in the finale and  that he hopes that those who love and  hate bakugou will enjoy it on top of  that toga and ochako will have a final  confrontation and understandably  shiguraki will be deku's biggest  obstacle as it's still unclear whether  or not midoriya will be able to save him  my honest thoughts on this series ending  next year is that based on where the  story is right now it makes sense but i  am slightly disappointed that the things  we'll likely never get to see for  example things like an internship in the  usa or a second sports festival or even  exploring the kids second and third  years at ua there's not really any time  to do that anymore because you know it'd  just be it would have to be squeezing at  the end and it just wouldn't be fleshed  out i guess what i'm trying to say is  that if my hero ends next year and we  never get a sequel series then i  personally feel like there's a lot of  things about this whole world that were  left unexplored however you gotta  respect the fact that hirokoshi is just  telling the story he wants to tell and  isn't milking it just for the sake of it  there's also the possibility that  there's a spin-off manga like my hero  academia vigilantes i mean that could  still be a thing after the main series  is done because hirokoshi himself  wouldn't necessarily have to do it we  also know that the studio loves to make  new movies i mean that will likely  continue long after the manga is done i  remember there was a rumor a long time  ago that they were meant to be like nine  or ten movies i think uh i don't know if  that was true but i mean we've been  getting movies every year so  possible that when the manga is complete  we'll still be getting movies for years  and years and years as long as the anime  keeps going at least  anyway guys let me know your thoughts in  the comments down below both about the  trailer and about my academia ending and  don't forget to s